# Store and check out every text file with LF, on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf is enabled on the author's machine, so without this a fresh
# clone would be handed CRLF and the next commit would show whole-file diffs.
#
# Note: some sources deliberately contain a NUL character (used as a
# composite-key separator, and exercised as a test value). Those are written
# as \0 escapes, not raw bytes, so git keeps treating them as text.
* text=auto eol=lf
